# Generated artifacts are never text-merged (issue #4058).
#
# merge=autospec-regen
#   Declares, by name, the merge driver that resolves a conflict on a
#   generated file by taking theirs instead of text-merging. A single-value
#   file (a hash golden) cannot survive a text merge: the losing side becomes
#   a second hash, and a build passes over the corruption. The driver's
#   output is a placeholder, not the answer: authoritative content comes
#   from running the owning generator after the merge (the conversion pass,
#   or by hand). Register the driver per clone:
#       bash scripts/register-regen-merge-driver.sh
#   Without registration git ignores the directive and text-merges the file,
#   i.e. exactly the corruption this declaration exists to prevent.
#
# generated-by=<script>
#   Machine-readable pointer to the owning generator (AC4), queryable with:
#       git check-attr generated-by -- <path>
#   The conversion pass builds its generator registry from these pointers
#   (see crates/autospec-core/src/conflict_resolution.rs) instead of
#   hard-coding artifact ownership. Every committed generated artifact
#   declared here is covered by tests/regen-merge-driver.bats.

tests/fixtures/skill-goldens/*.sha256 merge=autospec-regen generated-by=scripts/gen-skill-goldens.sh
config/generated-artifact-integrity.sha256 merge=autospec-regen generated-by=scripts/gen-harness-runtime-aliases.sh
templates/generated/harness-runtime-aliases.sh merge=autospec-regen generated-by=scripts/gen-harness-runtime-aliases.sh
templates/generated/harness-runtime-aliases.fish merge=autospec-regen generated-by=scripts/gen-harness-runtime-aliases.sh
docs/generated/harness-runtime-aliases.md merge=autospec-regen generated-by=scripts/gen-harness-runtime-aliases.sh
